ns":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LazySegmentTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MonoidAction","preciseIdentifier":"s:10RangeTrees12MonoidActionP","identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/MonoidAction","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The layout is "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/SegmentTree"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s: a perfect binary tree over the values padded to a power of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"two, in one flat array of cells. Beside each internal cell sits a pending update, applied to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that cell’s value but not yet to the cells below it. A range update applies itself to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") cells that cover the range and leaves it pending there, pushing older pending"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"updates down one level on the way so that updates reach each cell in the order they were made."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A query reads without changing the tree, composing the pending updates of the cells it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"passes through."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/MonoidAction","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" names the monoid and the updates:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["enum AddToSum: MonoidAction {","    typealias Values = Sum<Int>","    static var identity: Int { 0 }","    static func compose(_ outer: Int, _ inner: Int) -> Int { outer + inner }","    static func apply(_ update: Int, to sum: Int, count: Int) -> Int { sum + update * count }","}","","var tree = LazySegmentTree<AddToSum>([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])","tree.apply(10, in: 1 ..< 4)","tree.combined(in: 0 ..< 5)   \/\/ 45","tree[2]                      \/\/ 13"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As a collection, a lazy segment tree’s elements are the values, in order, with every update"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applied."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/rangetrees\/lazysegmenttree"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://RangeTrees/documentation/RangeTrees/LazySegmentTree/Equatable-Implementations":{"title":"Equatable Implementations","role":"collectionGroup","type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/rangetrees\/lazysegmenttree\/equatable-implementations","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree\/Equatable-Implementations"},"doc://RangeTrees/Sl":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/Sl","title":"Swift.Collection"},"doc://RangeTrees/documentation/RangeTrees/LazySegmentTree/Element":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree\/Element","title":"LazySegmentTree.Element","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Element","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/rangetrees\/lazysegmenttree\/element"},"doc:/